{"id": "9th-u8-q134", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "conceptual", "level": "comprehension", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "9th-tamil-u8", "lesson_id": "9th-tamil-u8-l5", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "anthathi-thodai-definition", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "ஓரடியின் இறுதி எழுத்தோ, அசையோ, சொல்லோ அடுத்த அடியின் தொடக்கமாக வருமாறு பாடுவது எது?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "செந்தொடை", "B": "அந்தாதித் தொடை", "C": "இரட்டைத் தொடை", "D": "மோனைத் தொடை"}, "explanation": "ஓரடியின் அந்தம் (முடிவு) அடுத்த அடியின் ஆதியாக (தொடக்கமாக) அமையப் பாடுவது 'அந்தாதித் தொடை' எனப்படும்."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the terminal letter, syllable, or word of a line becomes the initial element of the succeeding line, what is it called?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Sendhodai", "B": "Anthathi Thodai (அந்தாதித் தொடை - Anadiplosis / End-to-beginning linkage)", "C": "Irattai Thodai", "D": "Monai Thodai"}, "explanation": "Anthathi (Antham + Aadhi) links the ending of one verse directly to the beginning of the next."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "B", "accepted_keys": ["B"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 166, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil,